--- 4: is the difference attributable to T_0? ---------------------
    At weak contrast the two T_0 agree to 1.8e-5 yet both miss Kennett
    by 2.1e-3, so most of the error is SHARED and belongs to the
    lattice, not to T_0.  A difference in a mostly-shared error could
    be cancellation rather than accuracy.  The discriminator is
    whether the ratio survives refining the lattice: if the shared
    part falls while the ratio holds, the ratio is about T_0.
    M=  8   shared error at weak contrast 2.0755e-03    strong-contrast ratio fo/pkg 0.8987
    M= 12   shared error at weak contrast 1.6919e-03    strong-contrast ratio fo/pkg 0.8765
    M= 16   shared error at weak contrast 1.4452e-03    strong-contrast ratio fo/pkg 0.8569
    the ratio moves AWAY from unity as the shared error falls: True
    at the finest lattice the first-order error is 14.3% smaller,
    and still improving, so that figure is a lower bound.
  PASS  the advantage is not cancellation: it grows as the shared error falls
  PASS  the first-order T_0 is the more accurate of the two here

--- 5: which channel carries the improvement? ---------------------
    STRUCTURAL FACT FIRST.  effective_stiffness_voigt takes ONE
    Dmu*_off and writes it into all three shear slots, so the package's
    T_0 is cubic-symmetric by construction and CANNOT represent an
    e12/e13 split.  The symmetry-breaking part of the O(Dc^2)
    difference is therefore excluded from this comparison already --
    not by choice, but because there is no slot for it.  Of the four
    channels only theta touches x3 at all; e_diag = e11 - e22 and
    e_off = e12 are both x3-free.
    baseline (all Navier)                  err 3.7802e-02   ratio 1.0000
    first-order u       only               err 3.7802e-02   ratio 1.0000
    first-order theta   only               err 3.2393e-02   ratio 0.8569
    first-order e_diag  only               err 3.7802e-02   ratio 1.0000
    first-order e_off   only               err 3.7802e-02   ratio 1.0000
    all four first-order                   err 3.2393e-02   ratio 0.8569
    all four, but e13 in place of e12      err 3.2393e-02   ratio 0.8569
    the e12/e13 amplitude split itself is 7.201e-03
    so the discarded symmetry breaking is worth 0.000e+00 of the baseline error
  PASS  the improvement survives either choice of the split channel

--- 6: oblique incidence, where the shear channels are probed -----
    At p = 0 a normal-incidence P wave is pure compression along z: it
    couples to the trace and to nothing else, which is why every shear
    channel above moved R_PP by exactly zero.  SH incidence at p /= 0
    probes the shear channels directly, and is the only place the
    e12/e13 split can show at all.
    Kennett R_SH reference at p=1.0e-04
    baseline (all Navier)                  err 4.9763e-03   ratio 1.0000
    all four first-order, e12              err 4.9763e-03   ratio 1.0000
    all four first-order, e13              err 2.0248e-03   ratio 0.4069
    the choice between e12 and e13 is worth 5.931e-01 of the baseline error
  PASS  SH incidence does probe the shear channels

--- 7: a TETRAGONAL T_0, which can carry the split ----------------
